  "content": {
    "id": "p23-q14-root",
    "type": "question",
    "label": "14",
    "prompt": "The figure below shows a nested collection of squares. The vertices of the second largest square divide the sides of the largest square in the ratio $1:3$, and the vertices of the third largest square divide the sides of the second largest square in the ratio $1:3$, and so on.",
    "layout": "list",
    "columns": null,
    "questionDiagrams": [
      {
        "id": "p23-q14-diagram",
        "role": "question",
        "format": "tikz",
        "code": "% mathsmap-diagram-colours {\"version\":1,\"kind\":\"geometry\",\"base\":[],\"semantic\":[{\"name\":\"orangeFamily\",\"hex\":\"FCE8D5\",\"reason\":\"triangular family whose areas are requested\"},{\"name\":\"redFamily\",\"hex\":\"FCDFE1\",\"reason\":\"second congruent spiral family\"},{\"name\":\"purpleFamily\",\"hex\":\"E8DEF4\",\"reason\":\"third congruent spiral family\"},{\"name\":\"blueFamily\",\"hex\":\"D4E8FF\",\"reason\":\"fourth congruent spiral family\"}],\"reference\":\"source page 23, p23-q14-diagram\"}\n\\begin{tikzpicture}[x=1cm,y=1cm]\n\\special{dvisvgm:raw <metadata data-graph-strokes=\"1\"/>}\n\\definecolor{orangeFamily}{HTML}{FCE8D5}\n\\definecolor{redFamily}{HTML}{FCDFE1}\n\\definecolor{purpleFamily}{HTML}{E8DEF4}\n\\definecolor{blueFamily}{HTML}{D4E8FF}\n\\coordinate (A0) at (0,0);\n\\coordinate (B0) at (4,0);\n\\coordinate (C0) at (4,4);\n\\coordinate (D0) at (0,4);\n\\foreach \\n in {0,...,17}{\n\\pgfmathtruncatemacro{\\m}{\\n+1}\n\\coordinate (A\\m) at ($(A\\n)!0.75!(B\\n)$);\n\\coordinate (B\\m) at ($(B\\n)!0.75!(C\\n)$);\n\\coordinate (C\\m) at ($(C\\n)!0.75!(D\\n)$);\n\\coordinate (D\\m) at ($(D\\n)!0.75!(A\\n)$);\n\\fill[orangeFamily] (A\\n)--(A\\m)--(D\\m)--cycle;\n\\fill[blueFamily] (B\\n)--(B\\m)--(A\\m)--cycle;\n\\fill[purpleFamily] (C\\n)--(C\\m)--(B\\m)--cycle;\n\\fill[redFamily] (D\\n)--(D\\m)--(C\\m)--cycle;\n\\draw[black,line width=0.8pt] (A\\n)--(B\\n)--(C\\n)--(D\\n)--cycle;\n}\n\\draw[black,line width=0.8pt] (A18)--(B18)--(C18)--(D18)--cycle;\n\\node[above,text=black] at (0.5,4) {$1$};\n\\node[above,text=black] at (2.5,4) {$3$};\n\\node[right,text=black] at (4,3.5) {$1$};\n\\node[right,text=black] at (4,1.5) {$3$};\n\\node[below,text=black] at (1.5,0) {$3$};\n\\node[below,text=black] at (3.5,0) {$1$};\n\\node[left,text=black] at (0,2.5) {$3$};\n\\node[left,text=black] at (0,0.5) {$1$};\n\\end{tikzpicture}",
        "src": null,
        "widthMm": 65,
        "alt": "Mathematical diagram",
        "overlayOf": null,
        "transparent": false,
        "axes": null,
        "spec": {
          "sourcePage": 23,
          "sourceRegion": "Question 14 diagram, lower left column",
          "description": "Nested squares with cyclic 1:3 side subdivisions and four consistently coloured spirals of triangular regions. Eighteen nested stages represent the continuing construction. Source dark blue maps to house purple and cyan to house blue so the four families remain distinct.",
          "mathematics": "Outer square has side 4. Each next vertex lies three quarters of the way along the corresponding oriented side. Nested-square side lengths have ratio sqrt(10)/4 and areas have ratio 5/8. The orange family starts at the bottom-left corner.",
          "answerVisibility": "Only source givens and coloured regions are visible; no calculated areas or ratios are supplied."
